most Easter eggs are discovered within a  few weeks or months of a videogames  release but once in a while it takes a  little longer to find some of the secret  goodies developers bury within their  products  let's put saving Hyrule on hold while we  explore some Easter eggs that were  hidden a little too well and took a  whole lot longer to find halo 3 happy  birthday Lauren during Halo 3's creation  one of the developers sneaked in a  little message that took years to find  in fact he actually had to reveal the  secret himself after seven years since  no one had found it Adrian Perez  revealed in 2014 that he hid a secret  message in Halo 3's main loading screen  the only way to get it was to set your  consoles clock to December 25th or play  the game during this actual day and  press in both thumbsticks while the game  is loading happy birthday Lauren will  appear on the loading screen if done  correctly as cool as this little gift  might be it hardly makes up for the fact  that Lauren shares her birthday with  Christmas that's the worst  The Legend of Zelda a Link to the Past  Chris Houlihan's room in 1990 Nintendo  Power ran a contest that would allow a  fan to get their name included in an  unannounced SNES game which turned out  to be a Link to the Past it was revealed  in the early 2000s that the winner was a  fan named Chris Houlihan in order to see  his name you'd have to glitch link into  a secret room full of rupees and a  plaque that featured the lucky fans name  but as having your name hidden within an  impossible to find glitch really that  much of a prize maybe Chris would have  been better off taking whatever was  behind door number 2 Final Fantasy 9 the  Nero brothers quest despite being  released in 2000 Final Fantasy 9s final  quest was found a whopping 13 years  later this quest had players  encountering the Nero brothers as they  taught sadani the finer points of  gambling what made the secret so  difficult to track down was the fact  that you had to find them throughout  multiple points in the game in order to  continue with the quests progression and  after all that work you would have  received a protect ring as your reward a  solid if not particularly rare item yay  Batman Arkham City cow  under man's creepy message in Batman  Arkham City players can visit the  villain calendar man on different  holidays in the real world to listen to  some unique dialogue after the Easter  Egg remained undiscovered for three  years Rocksteady Studios intervened and  revealed how to discover this hidden bit  of dialogue here's the trick if you set  the date on your PC or console to  December 13 2004 the date Rocksteady  Studios was founded you get a message  that references Batman Arkham Knight the  next game in the series which at the  time hadn't even been announced yet I  was there at your beginning and I will  be there that's your pen the irony of  course is that calendar man is obsessed  with dates but he'll never actually  score a date himself just look at him  Splinter Cell double agent seals  Splinter Cell double agent was released  in 2006 but it wasn't until 2010 that  players learned courtesy of one of the  developers that they could find a secret  mission to rescue baby seals wearing  party hats they're just these cute  little things with names like pepperoni  and were beamed away after being rescued  because apparently they're aliens as  well wave race blue storm sarcastic  announcer wave race blue storm featured  an announcer who would provide color  commentary whenever players performed  cool tricks on their jet skis in 2009  eight years after its Gamecube release  it was discovered that players could  input a code on the audio settings  screen in order to activate an  alternative announcer one who was  decidedly more sarcastic as he raced he  would say things like it was great Mike  Tyson's punch-out ball Bulls tell now  here is an Easter Egg that actually  helps players out in Mike Tyson's  punch-out the Easter egg involves the  fight with bald bull and it wasn't  discovered for 22 years in 2009 former  Nintendo CEO Satoru Iwata revealed that  there was an easier way to beat bald  bull that didn't require you to punch  him after his third hop in order to  interrupt his bull charge all you had to  do was look at the background and try to  spot an audience member who was taking a  picture with a flash camera once the  flash went off you could deliver a body  blow to the bowl to bring him down that  would have saved NES gamers a lot of  misery back in the 80s well better late  than never right after all the retro  gamers out there learned about bald  Bulls tell a similar trick was found for  piston honda on april 8th 2016 Reddit  user and youtuber Midwestern housewives  discovered a visual cue that can help  Little Mac beat piston honda with ease  during your world circuitry match piston  honda will go for a barrage of hits and  will back step before charging veteran  gamers are well aware that you can  counter his delayed charge during the  sequence for a knockout but you must  have precise timing similar to the bald  bull trick watch the front of the crowd  on the left side a bearded audience  member will not duck the exact moment  you're supposed to counterpunch honda  this standout spectator also does the  same thing for bald bulls charged during  your rematch with him it's crazy to  think that another punch-out secret was  hiding in plain sight until it was  discovered 28 years after the game's NES  debut thanks for watching subscribe to  our YouTube channel to see more videos  like the one you just saw and leave us a  comment to let us know which secrets you  think should have made this list
 

